content.text:
The 404s came from a mismatch over who owns the `/api/v1` prefix. Compose passes `VITE_API_URL: http://localhost:3000` — just the origin — but the axios client treated that value as the complete base path, so every call hit `http://localhost:3000/organizations`, `/dashboard`, etc. The backend registers all feature routes under `/api/v1`, so those bare paths legitimately 404. It worked in neither container nor host mode; the fallback default was the only value that happened to include the prefix, and Compose always overrode it.

The fix keeps the env var meaning the origin and puts the prefix in the client:

```16:24:apps/frontend/src/resources/api.ts
/** `VITE_API_URL` is the API origin; the app prefix lives here. */
const apiOrigin = (
  import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL ?? 'http://localhost:3000'
).replace(/\/+$/, '');

export const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: apiOrigin.endsWith('/api/v1') ? apiOrigin : `${apiOrigin}/api/v1`,
});
```

This also covers the two ways the variable gets set in this repo: `.env.example` has the bare origin, and someone who instead writes a value already ending in `/api/v1` won't get a doubled prefix. Trailing slashes are trimmed so `http://localhost:3000/` doesn't produce `//api/v1`.

Verified against your running API: `GET /organizations` returns 404, while `/api/v1/organizations`, `/api/v1/dashboard`, and `/api/v1/documents?source=uploaded` all return 200. Format, typecheck, and lint pass.

The SSE calls for chat and brief generation build their URL from `api.defaults.baseURL`, so they pick this up too. Since the change is in source rather than the environment, Vite will hot-reload it — just refresh the tab at `localhost:5173`; no container restart needed.
